MID_SE_Bel_Tal_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_B_001: From White-Maned Demon to strapping king \nof Brezarant.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_B_002: Talimun, do you have something to say? I don't care\nto spend my time talking in circles.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_B_003: A trait we have in common then. I was simply\nmarveling at the new king of Brezarant's grandeur.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_B_004: I have five years behind me. I hardly think I'm a\n"new king."
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_B_005: A fair point! But five years for you is more of a...\nseason for me. I'm even older than your kingdom.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_B_006: Brezarant itself was founded in...1043, was it? \nI was born in 875, you see.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_B_007: So the wizened elder has come here to tease the\nyoung upstart?
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_B_008: Teasing? Heavens, no. I just thought you and I\nwould make fast friends.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_B_009: Brezarant's throne sits empty for years, and you just\nshow up and BAM. Not an easy thing to accomplish.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_B_010: One might even think this was a situation too good\nto be true. That, or this was some kind of setup.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_B_011: Hmm.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_B_012: Your land's history is a bloody one, indeed. There's\nthe Zodiac Incident for starters.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_B_013: And then you've got Hildebad's rule. The chaos he\nunleashed is enough to send shivers, don't you think?
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_B_014: He tried to claim his nephew had a right to the\nthrone, didn't he? Heh. Silly.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_B_015: So how will you grapple with a history like that? You,\nwith no strings tying you down. I'm dying to know.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_B_016: Governance isn't a performance for your amusement.\nThe choices I make affect people's lives.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_B_017: Truer words, Your Majesty. But choices naturally\nattract attention, you see.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_B_018: And all YOUR current choices are tied up in wars\nand foes in the shadows.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_B_019: Win a battle, you gain respect. Win another, you gain\nlove. But it never ends, does it?
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_B_020: You may find that maintaining peace you've earned\nis more challenging than winning it to begin with.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_B_021: I'm not too fussed about what's easy or hard, as long\nas I'm doing what's right.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_B_022: Which is exactly why we should be pals!
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_B_023: And as a token of our blossoming union, I'd like to\ngift you something from Vandahl Trading!
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_B_024: We pride ourselves on our wide selection of products!\nWe have famed horses, shields blessed by the spirits.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_B_025: Fine ghosh, the softest bedding on the market!\nJewelry for a lover, perhaps? Anything you like!
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_B_026: No need. I'm not wanting for anything.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_B_027: Hmph. He didn't even hesitate to say no! Winning\nthis king over will be tough...but not impossible.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_A_001: Talimun, a moment? I'd like to talk.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_A_002: Ah, I'm a bit tied up here, Majesty. What can I do\nfor you?
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_A_003: We can discuss it later. But you asked what I wanted\nfrom your company, and I came up with an answer.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_A_004: Oh, yes! The token of friendship. I'm honored\nyou remembered.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_A_005: Well, tell me—what in this world does the strong,\nvaliant king of Brezarant seek most?
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_A_006: It's you.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_A_007: M-me? Wait—what?!
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_A_008: You said you'd give me anything I wanted, right?\nWell, I want you as my partner.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_A_009: Well, well, you finally reveal your naughty side!\nI must say, that's quite the invitation...
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_A_010: You're long-lived—you know the wants of the\npeople. You'd make a great trading partner.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_A_011: Oop— You mean business! Of course, you did.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_A_012: Well, then?
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_A_013: Sorry, but I have to decline. I'm an adventurer whose\nonly true partner is his freedom.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_A_014: Being an exclusive merchant for one crown just isn't\nmy way. Heh. I'm nearly suffocating on the words.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_A_015: What happened to giving me anything? I thought\nmerchants honored their promises.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_A_016: Hahaha! I'm the head of a trading company,\nnot a product.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_A_017: Very well. In any case, I hope you and I can continue\nto work together.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_A_018: We'll need goods and manpower if we're to rebuild,\nand you have both.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_A_019: I've never considered myself a bleeding heart, but\nthere's plenty of reasons you and I should join forces.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_A_020: My business only prospers because of the people\nyou protect.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_A_021: I want my people to have peace and prosperity.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_A_022: Help me give them that, and you can consider your\npromise fulfilled.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_A_023: Eh, remind me not to be so loose with the word\n"anything" from now on.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_A_024: It's not cheap, enriching a country of people, you\nknow. One might even call you greedy.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_A_025: No, not greedy. Just jilted.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_A_026: Now I don't have anyone to share my bed\nwith tonight.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_A_027: What?! So you are making a move on me!
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_A_028: Haha. You're not the only one who likes teasing.
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_A_029: Urgh! Damn it! You— You shouldn't play with\npeople like that!
MID_SE_Bel_Tal_A_030: Flirting is supposed to be MY specialty!